      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from the Spanish word for grape, “uva,” after early explorers spotted wild grapes by the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
